      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed annealing treatments will not change the overall FeNiCrMn composition.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed annealing treatments will not alter the gross microstructure of FeNiCrMn.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The degree of SRO can be quantified by combining synchrotron XRD, TEM, and atom probe tomography.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "In FeNiCrMn, enhanced SRO inhibits dislocation activation and modifies dislocation slip behavior.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642976::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced SRO creates additional barriers that make dislocation motion tortuous or delayed.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642976::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced SRO alters the local energy landscape in FeNiCrMn.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Greater SRO increases the yield strength of FeNiCrMn.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642976::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Greater SRO increases the work-hardening rate of FeNiCrMn.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642976::web::004::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Greater SRO increases the strain-rate sensitivity of FeNiCrMn.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The influence of SRO is particularly strong when dislocation mobility is thermally activated.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism applies from 10^-2 to 10^3 s^-1 and from room temperature to 500 K.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Outside the specified strain-rate and temperature ranges, dynamic recovery or twinning may become dominant.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
